## Context

Surfaced during /verify of PR #200 (ticket 0158). The pytest-guard CI job
added in PR #194 (ticket 0154) is failing on main since PR #197 (ticket 0155)
removed the _BUILTIN_PROJECTS fallback.

Symptom: pytest-guard CI run 25851149946 fails because beat.py's
load_projects() does `sys.exit(1)` at module import when projects.json
is not found at the expected path. In CI, the path resolution differs
from local — the file exists at `scripts/projects.json` but the CI
working directory and HARNESS_DIR resolution may point elsewhere.

## Investigation needed

- Reproduce locally with `HARNESS_DIR=/tmp/empty pytest tests/`
- Check how CI sets HARNESS_DIR (env var? cwd?)
- Determine whether the fix is:
  a. Make load_projects() lazy (don't call at import time, only when needed)
  b. Set BEAT_PROJECTS_CONFIG env var in CI
  c. Add a tmp_path projects.json fixture for tests that trigger import

## Exit criteria

- [ ] pytest-guard CI job green on main
- [ ] All 223 tests pass in CI (currently pass locally)
- [ ] Root cause documented in commit message
